## Original Content
Kiran Abbavaram&#8217;s mythological action-fantasy for Zee Studios has revealed its title as &#8220;Indraputra,&#8221; with the pan-Indian project, directed by Srikanth Puppala, set to begin principal photography in October. Abbavaram takes on a mythology-rooted part built around the conflict between dharma, the principle of righteous duty and moral order in Hindu philosophy, and adharma, its violation. [&#8230;]

## Summary
Kiran Abbavaram's mythological action-fantasy film, titled 'Indraputra', directed by Srikanth Puppala, is set to start principal photography in October, exploring the conflict between dharma and adharma. The project is a pan-Indian venture backed by Zee Studios. Principal photography commencement is scheduled for October.

## Key Points
- Film title: 'Indraputra', a mythological action-fantasy starring Kiran Abbavaram
- Directed by Srikanth Puppala, produced by Zee Studios as a pan-Indian project
- Theme revolves around the conflict between dharma (righteous duty) and adharma (its violation) in Hindu philosophy
- Principal photography scheduled to begin in October


